 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Avatar Aang: All Four Elements",
 "notes": [
  "Plan: each bend draws a card with Aang out, including firebending, so every attacker with firebending replaces itself. Bend all four ways in one turn and he flips.",
  "The flip: Aang, Master of Elements makes spells cost {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} less, and at any upkeep you may flip him back to gain 4, draw 4, put four +1/+1 counters on him and deal 4 to each opponent. He can do that on an opponent's upkeep and flip again later.",
  "Cheapest route to all four: Aang attacks (fire), then Airbending Lesson (instant air), Sandbenders' Storm (instant earth), and North Pole Patrol or Katara (waterbend by tapping creatures).",
  "Color identity is all five, but the list casts no black spells. You can add black Avatar cards later without breaking legality.",
  "The Legend of Kyoshi draws off your largest power, so Aang, Zuko or a big earthbent land makes it a refill. It flips into Avatar Kyoshi, a mana engine that protects your lands.",
  "Aang's Shelter stays out: it's Teferi's Protection, a Game Changer.",
  "Estimated, not simulated: wins around turns 9–11, with a large flying Aang, the flip-back drain and land creatures. Early game is the deck's weak spot: four colors and many tapped lands, but cheap earthbend and Avatar's Wrath buy time.",
  "Rares and mythics to pick up or check your binder for: Aang, Swift Savior; Aang, at the Crossroads; Airbender Ascension; Avatar's Wrath; Birds of Paradise; Bumi, Unleashed; Chaos Warp; Earthbender Ascension; Exotic Orchard; Fabled Passage; Fire Nation Palace; Firebending Student; Heroic Intervention; Iroh, Grand Lotus; Katara, Water Tribe's Hope; Ran and Shaw; Temple of Abandon; Temple of Enlightenment; Temple of Mystery; Temple of Plenty; The Legend of Kyoshi; Toph, Hardheaded Teacher; Toph, the First Metalbender",
  "Commons and uncommons to pick up or check your binder for: Aang, the Last Airbender; Airbender's Reversal; Airbending Lesson; Appa, Loyal Sky Bison; Badgermole; Beast Within; Bender's Waterskin; Bitter Work; Command Tower; Crashing Wave; Cultivate; Earth Kingdom General; Earth Rumble; Earthbending Lesson; Earthbending Student; Energybending; Enter the Avatar State; Evolving Wilds; Farseek; Fire Nation Attacks; Fire Sages; Flexible Waterbender; Frontier Bivouac; Generous Gift; Glider Staff; Harrow; Haru, Hidden Talent; Jungle Shrine; Katara, Bending Prodigy; Kodama's Reach; Kyoshi Village; Meditation Pools; Mystic Monastery; Nature's Lore; North Pole Gates; North Pole Patrol; Omashu City; Origin of Metalbending; Path of Ancestry; Rocky Rebuke; Sandbenders' Storm; Seaside Citadel; Sun Warriors; Terramorphic Expanse; The Boulder, Ready to Rumble; Toph, the Blind Bandit; Uncle Iroh; Waterbending Lesson; Zuko, Exiled Prince"
 ],
